<title>BRAZIL: Brazil soybean cargo heading for U.S. - agent.</title>
<headline>Brazil soybean cargo heading for U.S. - agent.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The vessel Kardamyla left the Brazilian port of Paranagua with 53,362 tonnes of soybeans on March 31 destined for the port of New Orleans, La., said shipping agent Transcar.</p>
<p>&quot;It went to the U.S. to New Orleans,&quot; said an agent at Transcar. &quot;The exporter was Louis Dreyfus.&quot;  </p>
<p>The exporter said he did not know when the vessel was scheduled to arrive.</p>
<p>One U.S. exporter said, &quot;The rumor in the market is that it is supposed to arrive in New Orleans around the middle of April.&quot;</p>
<p>He added, &quot;There are rumors of other possible boats coming but I have no way of confirming that. I'm fairly sure the boat arriving in the middle of April is the real thing.&quot; </p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
